Spec: OperatorLib

Purpose:
  Anchor the `controller` library of the `operator` crate: declare the module tree the
    reconciling controller runs on — the shared instance algorithm, the three instance kinds,
    the JukeBox scan, @Manager, telemetry and the private @metrics module — and own the
    crate-wide @Reconciler contract every custom resource implements plus the identity
    surfaces @OPERATOR and @get_client_name. The crate root is the whole import surface of the
    separate `operator` binary, which pulls it via @controller in ./main.rs; the re-exported
    @Error, @Result, @Manager and the four CR models are what that binary and every in-crate
    @crate path then name. Module behaviour itself belongs to each module spec, referenced
    below.

Owns:
  ./lib.rs

References:
  ./instance_common.sdd, ./instanceservice.sdd, ./instancesystem.sdd, ./instancetenant.sdd,
    ./jukebox.sdd, ./manager.sdd, ./main.rs — specs pending; their owners own the module and
    binary behaviour this file only declares and re-exports.
  ./metrics.sdd, ./telemetry.sdd — module specs; @metrics and @telemetry behaviour lives
    there, this file only fixes their visibility.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — source of @Error, @Result and the four re-exported CR models.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @common::get_client_name and its executable-derived client names;
    the divergence from this file's @get_client_name is frozen in Handles.
  /linting.sdd — the static-analysis harness whose per-crate `cfg_attr` form these crate
    attributes carry.

Must:
  Carry exactly the two crate attributes, in order:
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used))]`
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), warn(clippy::arithmetic_side_effects, clippy::indexing_slicing))]`
    Both lints are scoped to not(test), so the `cfg(test)` build runs without them.
  Declare seven `pub mod` modules: @instance_common, @instanceservice, @instancesystem,
    @instancetenant and @jukebox plain, @manager doc-commented
    `/// State machinery for kube, as exposeable to actix`, @telemetry doc-commented
    `/// Log and trace integrations`.
  Declare @metrics as the single private module — `mod metrics;` doc-commented `/// Metrics`
    — publishing @Metrics as its only crate-root name through @pub; every other item of
    ./metrics.rs stays reachable only as a @crate:: path inside this package (./metrics.sdd
    freezes the internal consumers).
  Carry exactly eight name-only re-exports at the crate root: the grouped @pub from @common of
    @Error, @Result and the CR models @ServiceInstance, @SystemInstance, @TenantInstance and
    @JukeBox, plus @Manager from @manager and @Metrics from @metrics. Nothing else reaches the
    root — in particular @common::get_client_name is not re-exported, so the root's
    @get_client_name resolves to this crate's own fn.
  Define @Reconciler as a `#[async_trait]` `pub trait` with exactly two async methods taking
    `&self` and @std::sync::@Arc<@manager::@Context> and returning @Result<@Action> with
    @Action from @kube::runtime::@controller: @Reconciler::reconcile and @Reconciler::cleanup.
    The re-exported @Result makes @Error the fixed failure type of both methods.
  Keep the @Reconciler implementations and dispatch where they are: all four root CR types
    implement the trait — @JukeBox in ./jukebox.rs, @ServiceInstance in ./instanceservice.rs,
    @SystemInstance in ./instancesystem.rs, @TenantInstance in ./instancetenant.rs — and the
    trait methods run only from the finalizer match arms of @run_with_finalizer, bounded
    @InstanceKind + @Reconciler, and of the jukebox finalizer wrapper (./instance_common.rs,
    ./jukebox.rs) reached from the ./manager.rs controller wiring; @dyn dispatch of the trait
    exists nowhere in the workspace.
  Pin @OPERATOR as a `pub static` of type `&str` with the exact value
    `operator.vynil.solidite.fr`.
  Define @get_client_name as a `#[must_use]` `pub` fn taking nothing and returning the literal
    `controller.vynil.solidite.fr` on every call, reading no environment or process state; the
    three @PatchParams::apply SSA lanes of the crate (./instance_common.rs, ./jukebox.rs)
    import this fn through the crate root, never the executable-derived @common twin.
  Run no code and hold no state beyond the static: no constructor, registration, global
    initialisation or @cfg test module lives here; the tokio runtime build, rustls provider
    install, tracing setup, @wire_core_k8s call and controller wiring all belong to @main in
    ./main.rs, and the @Manager/@Context construction to ./manager.rs.
  Keep the lib/bin target split: this root is lib target `controller` named in ../Cargo.toml,
    the `operator` bin is a separate crate that pulls it wholesale with
    `pub use controller::*` in ./main.rs, and in-crate modules reach these same names through
    @crate paths; dropping a `pub` here removes the name from both consumers at once.

Exposes:
  Modules @instance_common, @instanceservice, @instancesystem, @instancetenant, @jukebox,
    @manager, @telemetry — `pub mod`; behaviour of each owned by the referenced spec.
  @Reconciler — `pub` async_trait trait with @Reconciler::reconcile and
    @Reconciler::cleanup per the Must signature.
  @OPERATOR — `pub static` of type `&str`, value `operator.vynil.solidite.fr`.
  @get_client_name — `#[must_use] pub fn @get_client_name() -> @String`.
  Re-exports at crate root: @Error and @Result from @common; @ServiceInstance from
    @common::instanceservice, @SystemInstance from @common::instancesystem, @TenantInstance
    from @common::instancetenant, @JukeBox from @common::jukebox; @Manager aliasing
    @manager::@Manager; @Metrics aliasing @crate::metrics::@Metrics — the module-private
    type's only external name.

Accepts:
  This file branches on no input — every item is a module declaration, a re-export binding,
    the trait, the static or a nullary fn; @get_client_name has no arguments and no
    precondition in any feature or runtime state.

Returns:
  @get_client_name returns exactly `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`, identical on every call in
    every environment.

Handles:
  Two client-name lanes crossing the cluster: the crate's own @PatchParams::apply SSA field
    manager takes this file's invariant string, while @wire_core_k8s in ./main.rs registers
    @common::get_client_name into `vynil-core` — for the shipped `operator` binary both lanes
    resolve to `controller.vynil.solidite.fr` (that is the common fn's mapping of executable
    name `operator`), so the split is invisible in production; any other executable name —
    test harness, renamed binary — makes the common lane fall back to `vynil.solidite.fr`
    while this file keeps the `controller.` value.
  @OPERATOR — declared with no reader: no code, test, log line or annotation in the workspace
    names it.

Depends on:
  @common — path dependency `../common` in ../Cargo.toml: the @Error, @Result and four CR
    models this root mirrors.
  @async-trait `0.1.68` (../Cargo.toml) — the `#[async_trait]` attribute on @Reconciler.
  @kube — @kube::runtime::controller::@Action as both methods' success value (workspace kube,
    locked in /Cargo.lock).
  @std::sync::@Arc — the @Context carrier in both method signatures.
  ./manager.rs and ./metrics.rs — the two local modules whose @Manager and @Metrics names this
    root binds.
  ./main.rs — the `operator` bin crate; sole external consumer of this root surface via
    `pub use controller::*`.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the frozen root surface: the eight root names denote the same items as their
      @common/@module paths, @get_client_name returns its literal regardless of environment,
      and @OPERATOR carries its value. No mapped test exists — the ./jukebox.rs tests exercise
      that type's @Reconciler impl, not this file.
  [?] @OPERATOR is dead — zero use sites — and its value `operator.vynil.solidite.fr` is a
      third spelling matching nothing in use: the actual SSA field manager is
      @get_client_name's `controller.vynil.solidite.fr` and the CRD group is
      `vynil.solidite.fr`. Decide later whether the static is removed or wired in.
  [?] @get_client_name hard-codes at the crate root what @common::get_client_name derives from
      the executable, keeping both only because the shipped binary is named `operator`; the
      divergence and the executable-name scheme are already `[?]`-ed in
      /common/src/context.sdd. Decide later which file owns operator write identity: the
      crate-local copy or the shared dynamic fn.
  [?] The parent ./operator.sdd `Structure` describes this file as "Library root re-exporting
      the controllers and @InstanceKind", but this root re-exports neither controller funcs
      nor @InstanceKind — both are reachable only through their `pub mod` paths. Decide later
      whether the parent wording or a wider root surface is intended; the parent spec is not
      edited here.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, the identity
    decision is recorded, and `cargo test -p operator` with clippy, fmt and `specdd lint` are
    green.

Scenario: Crate-root names alias their source items
  Given an @Error, a @Result, one CR model, an @Manager and a @Metrics named through their
    @common or module paths
  When the same five are named at this crate root instead
  Then they are the same items and types, not copies or wrappers, and the root exposes nothing
    beyond the seven modules plus those eight names
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: get_client_name is constant while the common twin follows the binary
  Given any executable name and environment — `operator`, a cargo-test harness, a renamed
    binary
  When @get_client_name runs
  Then the result is always `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`
  But @common::get_client_name returns `vynil.solidite.fr` for every executable name other
    than `operator` and `agent`, so outside the shipped `operator` and `agent` binaries the
    two client names diverge
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Every kind runs through the Reconciler contract
  Given the four controller wires in ./manager.rs starting from the module-level @reconcile
    free functions
  When a watch event reaches a kind
  Then the module free fn hands the object to its finalizer wrapper — @run_with_finalizer for
    the three instance kinds, @reconcile's own wrapper for JukeBox — which dispatches
    @Reconciler::reconcile on Apply and @Reconciler::cleanup on Cleanup
  And a future kind joins that lane only by implementing both @Reconciler and @InstanceKind
  Partial coverage only: the ./jukebox.rs tests call @Reconciler::reconcile and
    @Reconciler::cleanup on @JukeBox; no test maps this trait contract across kinds.

Example:
  `@get_client_name()` in any process → `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`
  `@OPERATOR` value `operator.vynil.solidite.fr` — reaches no request and no label today
